  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory places Rumakan to the west of Veh-Ardashir. Morony puts it \"probably between the city of V\u0113h-Artakhshatr and S\u0101b\u0101t\u0323\". Obermeyer suggests that it was situated near Mehuza.</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "An ancient settlement or region of Babylonia whose precise location cannot be determined today. It was established as a tax-collection sub-district of V\u0113h-Artakhshatr by Ardash\u012br I. This place was also called Rumae and is referred to in the Babylonian Talmud, Treatise Megillah 26b, as having had a Jewish community.",
